      "writtenOn": "2025-01-31T23:36:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, it ought to work. `virtmgr` doesn\u0027t know the file path, only the FD, then it passes it along to `crosvm` as a `/proc/self/fd/...` path. We use the same trick for the disk files, kernel image, etc (some of those use `open_file_or_duplicate`, which special cases `/proc/self/fd/...`, but I think that isn\u0027t really needed for this one)",
      "parentUuid": "2df9e559_1506d437",
      "revId": "c18a9b3b5f24c41e35cf95562a2c1bbc59de543e",
